1
00:00:04,698 --> 00:00:09,903
Whiskers and Luna's World. Episode ten. Day and Night, Earth and Sun!

2
00:00:17,737 --> 00:00:20,705
One morning, the Sun was just coming up.

3
00:00:20,905 --> 00:00:24,430
Good morning, Sun. Where were you all night? Napping somewhere?

4
00:00:29,328 --> 00:00:34,855
Hoo-hoo! Good morning! I'm Professor Hoot. I was up all night, so now it's my bedtime.

5
00:00:35,055 --> 00:00:38,812
The Sun went nowhere! Pip, shine this torch on the globe.

6
00:00:42,536 --> 00:00:45,980
The side facing the light has day. The other side has night!

7
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:50,568
The Earth spins around once a day. One turn takes twenty-four hours.

8
00:00:58,402 --> 00:01:01,710
Twenty-four hours? That's how long my naps are.

9
00:01:04,553 --> 00:01:06,599
Hoo! Come and see it from space!

10
00:01:17,370 --> 00:01:19,673
Wow! The Earth is half bright, half dark!

11
00:01:19,873 --> 00:01:22,781
The Earth spins like a top. Watch our home.

12
00:01:27,092 --> 00:01:29,302
Here comes the sunlight. Sunrise!

13
00:01:34,787 --> 00:01:36,903
And now we turn away. Sunset!

14
00:01:37,103 --> 00:01:40,037
So the Sun only looks like it moves, because we spin!

15
00:01:41,999 --> 00:01:44,533
No more sunsets! I'll stop the Earth!

16
00:01:54,717 --> 00:01:55,995
Wheee! I'm dizzy!

17
00:01:56,195 --> 00:01:58,669
Hoo! The Earth is far too big to stop.

18
00:01:58,869 --> 00:02:01,717
I knew that. I was testing it. On purpose.

19
00:02:04,853 --> 00:02:09,935
When it's day on one side of the world, it's night on the other. Let's visit a friend!

20
00:02:16,595 --> 00:02:19,752
On the magic map, the night side was dark.

21
00:02:36,983 --> 00:02:41,274
Hello again, little travellers! It's bedtime here in Hawaii.

22
00:02:41,474 --> 00:02:43,414
But at home, it's breakfast time!

23
00:02:43,614 --> 00:02:46,411
Every place has its own time. Goodnight!

24
00:02:53,659 --> 00:02:56,521
Look, in the water! The Moon Fish is back!

25
00:03:00,832 --> 00:03:03,572
Whiskers, it's only the Moon, shining in the water!

26
00:03:03,772 --> 00:03:06,473
I know. This time, my paws stay dry.

27
00:03:06,673 --> 00:03:09,199
And the Moon has a secret. Up we go!

28
00:03:15,859 --> 00:03:20,176
The Moon makes no light. Sunlight bounces off it, like a mirror.

29
00:03:25,075 --> 00:03:27,135
So moonlight is really sunlight!

30
00:03:27,335 --> 00:03:30,119
The Moon goes around the Earth about once a month.

31
00:03:37,954 --> 00:03:41,777
So we see more or less of its sunny side. That's why it changes shape!

32
00:03:47,850 --> 00:03:52,800
And the Earth goes around the Sun once a year. Three hundred and sixty-five days!

33
00:04:02,397 --> 00:04:05,103
So every birthday, I've been once around the Sun!

34
00:04:05,303 --> 00:04:07,939
Then I want birthday cake. In space.

35
00:04:13,131 --> 00:04:18,277
Remember! One. The Earth spins around once a day. That makes day and night.

36
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:24,206
Two. The Earth goes around the Sun once a year.

37
00:04:27,049 --> 00:04:30,039
Three. The Moon shines with light from the Sun.

38
00:04:36,699 --> 00:04:42,152
Quiz time! At night, is the Sun gone, or is our side facing away from it?

39
00:04:45,288 --> 00:04:48,405
Facing away! The Sun never stops shining.

40
00:04:50,954 --> 00:04:53,377
Next. Where does moonlight come from?

41
00:04:56,513 --> 00:04:59,435
From the Sun! The Moon is like a mirror.

42
00:05:05,507 --> 00:05:07,731
What a season! Let's look back.

43
00:05:07,931 --> 00:05:13,034
Our round planet, seven continents, five oceans, mountains, and rivers.

44
00:05:13,234 --> 00:05:18,212
Deserts, rainforests, the frozen poles, the seasons, and day and night!

45
00:05:29,571 --> 00:05:32,946
Hoo! Now it's my turn to be awake. Goodnight, friends!

46
00:05:33,146 --> 00:05:35,210
Thank you for exploring the world with us!

47
00:05:35,410 --> 00:05:39,196
Next season? Sure. After a nap. A whole season long.

48
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:45,991
The end of season one. See you next season!

